B.aLS=new A.l2("dashcn","dashcn --help","dashcn <command> [arguments]","dashcn CLI","dashcn CLI\nUsage: dashcn <command> [arguments]\n\nComponents\n  add                     Install one or more components, blocks or flows and their closure.\n  eject                   Turn a package-mode component into owned sources.\n  remove (alias: rm)      Remove installed components, blocks, flows and orphaned layer files.\n  update                  Update installed components from the registry.\n  dry-run                 Preview what add would install (components, blocks, flows).\n  list (alias: ls)        List available components, blocks or flows, by category.\n  search                  Search components, blocks and flows by name, description or tag.\n  info (alias: i)         Show a component's, block's or flow's closure, files and api.\n\nProject\n  init                    Install the layer core and generate the app theme.\n  registries              List configured and discoverable registries.\n  default                 Set or show the default registry namespace.\n  sync                    Re-apply the installed closure and locked theme.\n  project                 Project repair and cleanup commands.\n  theme                   List and apply registry theme presets.\n\nDiagnostics\n  reset                   Clear global CLI-managed cache and home-directory state.\n  doctor                  Diagnose the manifest, closure, layout and lock drift.\n  validate                Validate the registry manifest against the v2 schema.\n  audit                   Compare installed files against dashcn.lock.\n\nTooling\n  feedback                Submit feedback or report issues.\n  version                 Show the CLI version.\n  upgrade                 Upgrade the CLI to the latest version.\n\nGlobal flags\n  General:\n    --verbose               Verbose logging\n    --version               Show the CLI version\n    --offline               Disable network calls (use cache only)\n\n  Registry Selection:\n    --registry-name         Registry namespace (e.g. dashcn)\n    --registry <path|url>   Registry source override",B.bM4)
