B.aM0=new A.l2("dashcn theme","dashcn theme --help","dashcn theme list [--json]","app_theme.dart is yours: without --refresh a locally modified file is",'Usage: dashcn theme list [--json]\n       dashcn theme apply <preset> [--refresh] [--json]\n       dashcn theme import <file|url> [--name <id>] [--apply]\n       dashcn theme export [--format css|tailwind|dtcg|json|dart]\n                           [--out <file>]\n       dashcn theme\n\nCommands:\n  list              Show the presets from the registry manifest\n  apply <preset>    Generate <installRoot>/theme/app_theme.dart\n  import <file|url> Store a web theme as <installRoot>/theme/<id>.json\n  export            Print the current theme in a web format\n\nOptions:\n  --refresh         Overwrite app_theme.dart even when it was edited\n  --json            Machine-readable output on stdout\n  --name <id>       Preset id for an import (default: file name)\n  --apply           Apply an import straight to app_theme.dart\n  --format <name>   Export format: css|tailwind|dtcg|json|dart\n  --out <file>      Write the export to a file instead of stdout\n  --help, -h        Show this message\n\napp_theme.dart is yours: without --refresh a locally modified file is\nreported as drift and left untouched.\n\nAn import needs no registry: CSS, Tailwind v3 configs and preset JSON\nparse into a stored preset; --apply renders it without one either.\n\nLegacy flags --apply/-a and --list still work. --apply-file,\n--apply-url and "theme widget" were removed with the v1 theme\nmanifest; use "theme import <file|url>" instead.',B.bCR)
